# MatPotLib backend — manual API tests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP).
# Fill in the variables below, then send requests individually.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
# Supabase access token (JWT) of a signed-in user
@jwt = REPLACE_WITH_SUPABASE_JWT
# Device provisioning values (see DEPLOYMENT.md device provisioning step)
@deviceId = REPLACE_WITH_DEVICE_UUID
@deviceToken = REPLACE_WITH_DEVICE_SECRET
@claimCode = REPLACE_WITH_CLAIM_CODE
# Filled after creating a plant / picking a species
@plantId = REPLACE_WITH_PLANT_UUID
@speciesId = REPLACE_WITH_SPECIES_UUID

### Health check (no auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ---------------- Profiles ----------------

### Get my profile (bootstraps an empty row on first call)
GET {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Update my profile (onboarding quiz answers)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/profiles/me
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "display_name": "Justin",
  "experience_level": "beginner",
  "goals": ["keep plants alive", "learn"],
  "plant_types": ["ferns", "succulents"]
}

### ---------------- Push ----------------

### Register Expo push token
POST {{baseUrl}}/push/register
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expo_token": "ExponentPushToken[xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx]",
  "platform": "ios"
}

### ---------------- Devices ----------------

### Claim a device by claim code (409 if invalid/claimed/already own one)
POST {{baseUrl}}/devices/claim
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "claim_code": "{{claimCode}}"
}

### List my devices
GET {{baseUrl}}/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Unlink (unclaim) a device I own
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/devices/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### ---------------- Species ----------------

### Search species (ilike on common/scientific name + aliases;
### falls back to LLM enrichment when nothing matches and OPENAI_API_KEY is set)
GET {{baseUrl}}/species?q=fern
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### ---------------- Plants ----------------

### List my plants (each with species + latest reading)
GET {{baseUrl}}/plants
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Add a plant
POST {{baseUrl}}/plants
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nickname": "Ferny",
  "device_id": "{{deviceId}}",
  "plant_species_id": "{{speciesId}}",
  "notes": "Lives on the kitchen windowsill"
}

### Plant detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/plants/{{plantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Edit a plant
PUT {{baseUrl}}/plants/{{plantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nickname": "Fern II",
  "notes": "Moved to the living room"
}

### Remove a plant
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/plants/{{plantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### ---------------- Sensors ----------------

### Device ingest (device token auth, not JWT — this is what the ESP32 sends)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
x-device-token: {{deviceToken}}

{
  "device_id": "{{deviceId}}",
  "moisture": 42.5,
  "temp_c": 21.3,
  "humidity": 55,
  "lux": 1200,
  "battery_pct": 88
}

### Ingest an out-of-range reading (should create an alert + push)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/readings
Content-Type: application/json
x-device-token: {{deviceToken}}

{
  "device_id": "{{deviceId}}",
  "moisture": 2,
  "temp_c": 21.3,
  "humidity": 55,
  "lux": 1200
}

### Latest reading for my device
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{deviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### Reading history for a chart window
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{deviceId}}/history?from=2026-07-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-07-04T23:59:59Z
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}

### ---------------- Alerts ----------------

### Alert history (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
